  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.678). The key evidence shows: (1) scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 by ~4pp, (2) weighted fusion > concat, (3) avgpool > transformer, and (4) image-only results suggest imagenet_vit_l (0.227) slightly edges resnet50 (0.208). The main untested dimension in the multimodal setting is the image encoder. Config_037 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This cleanly isolates whether a stronger pretrained image representation provides additional signal when fused with the already-strong scvi_n200 RNA features. It is the highest-value next experiment because it either extends the current best or confirms resnet50 is sufficient, reducing the search space for all subsequent image-encoder decisions."
